{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Kora (gasless fee payer for Solana)",
    "version": "2.2.0",
    "description": "Kora is a Solana fee payer: it signs a transaction as the fee payer so the user needs no SOL, and charges for it in a token instead.\n\nPROVENANCE. Kora publishes no usable specification. Its own generator emits OpenAPI 3.1.0 with 30 schemas and zero operations, because every method is POST / with a JSON-RPC envelope and OpenAPI cannot express many operations on one path. This document is RECOVERED FROM SOURCE: the request and response structs in crates/lib/src/rpc_server/method/*.rs and the method table in rpc.rs, at kora 2.2.0-beta.8. Three things in it were verified against a running node on 2026-09-07 and appear in no document: the server accepts a per-method path (POST /getVersion answers exactly as POST / does), parameters are NAMED and positional parameters are refused, and a no-argument method takes an empty object."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080",
      "description": "a Kora node you run"
    }
  ],
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "apiKeyAuth": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "header",
        "name": "x-api-key",
        "description": "Optional. Set only when the node configures kora.auth.api_key."
      }
    }
  },
